Intervals

      Merge
              Sort by start time, then linearly combine adjacent segments whenever the current start overlaps the previous end
              LC 57
      
      Delete
              Sort by end time to greedily keep intervals that finish earliest, dropping any subsequent intervals that conflict.
              LC 1272
      
      Sweep Line
              Flatten intervals into chronological +1 (start) and -1 (end) events, tracking peak concurrency or 
              metadata changes as you slide left-to-right
              LC 218
      
      Intersection
              Use two pointers to slide across two separate pre-sorted lists, grabbing the [max(starts), min(ends)] overlap window, 
              then advance the smaller end
              LC 986
      
      Complement
              Run a global merge on all schedules, then collect the empty time frames between the end of one merged block 
              and the start of the next
              LC 759
